{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 3: The XOR Problem",
  "description": "XOR: Output ON when inputs DIFFER (one high, one low).\n\nTHE PROBLEM: Try all possible weight combinations in a single-layer \nnetwork (like AND/OR gates). You'll find it's IMPOSSIBLE!\n\nXOR truth table:\n  0 XOR 0 = 0\n  0 XOR 1 = 1  \n  1 XOR 0 = 1\n  1 XOR 1 = 0\n\nTHE SOLUTION: This network has a HIDDEN LAYER (2 neurons).\nThe hidden neurons learn intermediate features:\n  - One learns \"A AND NOT B\"\n  - One learns \"B AND NOT A\"  \n  - Combined: gives XOR!\n\nThis is WHY deep networks are powerful - they can compute \nfunctions that single layers cannot.\n\nHistorical note: The XOR problem stumped AI for years until \nbackpropagation was popularized in the 1980s.",
  "metadata": {
