    {
      "id": "comment-f6de0b8e-594e-4fb4-bdbf-25927a3c30ff",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "name": "Welcome",
      "position": [
        50,
        50
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": "# XOR - The Problem That Changed History\n\nXOR (exclusive or) outputs ON when inputs are **different**.\n\n## Why XOR Matters\n\nIn 1969, Minsky & Papert proved a single neuron CAN'T learn XOR.\nThis \"killed\" neural network research for 15 years!\n\n## To Do and Notice\n\n1. **Try all combinations**: Notice XOR needs (0,1) and (1,0) ON, but (0,0) and (1,1) OFF\n2. **The hidden layer**: See how we need TWO neurons working together?\n3. **Think geometrically**: XOR points can't be separated by a single line\n\n## The Solution\n\nWe need a **hidden layer** - neurons that compute intermediate features.\nThe breakthrough came when backpropagation let us train these hidden layers.\n\n**Challenge**: Trace the values through both paths. How do they combine?",
        "width": 450,
        "show_on_start": true
      },
      "inputs": {},
      "outputs": {},
      "weights": {},
      "collapsed": false,
      "color": "#5c4a3d",
      "tags": [],
      "description": "Tutorial introduction"
    }
  ],
